  "decision_reason": "Rational query medians improve by 51\u201371% in the short probe, with first-query allocations reduced from 887 to one per 1,000 results. Other rows vary substantially, including unchanged construction work; a separately retained fourfold larger timing probe preserves all exact answers and the rational benefit but does not resolve symbolic regressions. Assembly shows an extra out-of-line coordinate helper on the fallback path. This implementation is not admitted.",
  "next_step": "Inline the coordinate helper and repeat the focused gate and matched costs. Replace test-only cached-interval API calls with the established certified-interval API so any successful point-only change can be isolated over admitted production source. No production checkout or full-board admission has been run.",
  "limitations": "Five fresh processes per version and mode, CPU 0, alternating order. No counting allocator in timing binaries; memory counts requested Rust bytes and excludes allocator metadata/native heaps. Eight point families, including shared-handle and copied-coordinate controls. First is a new pair, not empty global caches. Construction and explicit numerical preparation are measured separately. This scalar/point early gate does not admit full application behavior or production source.",
